Pruning can be categorized into two types: unstructured and structured. Unstructured pruning eliminates individual weights, whereas structured pruning removes entire neurons or layers. While unstructured pruning can yield higher compression ratios, it is difficult to implement on hardware due to the resulting irregular memory access patterns. In contrast, structured pruning is more practical for deployment.

